%U A399779 16,16,16,17,17,18,18,18,18,18,18,19,19,19,19,20,20,21,21,21,21,21,21,22,22,22,22,23
%N A399779 Maximum size of a subset S of {1,...,n} such that x does not divide y*z for any x,y,z in S with x != y and x != z.
%C A399779 The factors y and z are allowed to be equal, as explicitly stated by Chojecki (2026). Consequently, for distinct x,y in S, the condition that x does not divide y^2 is also required.
%C A399779 a(1) = 1, whereas A000720(1) = 0. For 2 <= n <= 104, a(n) = A000720(n). The next difference occurs at n = 105, where a(105) = 28 and A000720(105) = 27.
%H A399779 Seiichi Manyama, <a href="/A399779/b399779.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..127</a>
%H A399779 T. F. Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/793">Erdős Problem 793</a>.
%H A399779 Tsz Ho Chan, Jared Duker Lichtman, and Carl Pomerance, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s00493-021-4695-2">On the critical exponent for k-primitive sets</a>, Combinatorica 42 (2022), no. 5, 729-747.
%H A399779 Przemek Chojecki, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.15306">The Second Term for Strongly 2-Primitive Sets</a>, arXiv:2607.15306 [math.NT] (2026).
%F A399779 a(p) = a(p-1) + 1 if p is odd prime.
%Y A399779 Cf. A000720.
%K A399779 nonn,new
%O A399779 1,3
%A A399779 _Seiichi Manyama_, Sep 10 2026
